  "text": "Allergies:\nReglan / Imitrex / Morphine\n\nChief Complaint:\n\"I was having a pancreatitis flare and was in a\nlot of pain.\"\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nBriefly, this is a ___ y/o woman\nwith numerous medical comorbities, most notably including \nchronic\npancreatitis, as well as long-standing depression and anxiety \nwho\npresents with suicidal ideation in the context of pain from a\npancreatitis flare. She states tonight that she \"decided to\nbecome proactive\" about seeking admission to ___ because she\nknew she would not be safe on a medical unit. She notes that her\noutpatient therapist has been helping to improve her mood and \nshe\nhas been experiencing increases in her energy and concentration\nbut notes that her sleep has remained poor, as has her ability \nto\ndeal with her pain. She states that she currently recieves her\nmedications from her PCP, but intends to follow with a\npsychiatrist at her therapist's office in the near future.\nOverall, she describes herself as continuing to be depressed,\nanxious, seeking additional pain control, and unable to contract\nfor safety outside of the hospital. She is, however, happy to be\nback on Deac4 and is help-seeking.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ woman with hx of chronic pancreatitis and PPHx significant\nfor depression and anxiety with attempted suicide presenting \nwith depression, anxiety, and suicidality.\n\n#) Psychiatric.  Mood disorder NOS. Patient has a a history of \nchronic pancreatitis complicated by chronic abdominal pain with \nfrequent medical admissions for pain control, history of opiate \nmisuse, depression, and anxiety, who was re-admitted to \n___ after feeling unsafe at home. This is the pt's ___ \nDeac 4 admission this ___, and her ongoing pain makes her \nvulnerable to depression nos, anxiety, and suicide. The pt has \nbeen previosuly ambivalent about her detox and pain management, \nalthough she presents with renewed interest in getting help.\nShe is motivated to start suboxone and taper off methadone.   Pt \nis protected from suicide by her relationship with a stable \npartner, and the fact that she has a son. On presentation, \npatient was preoccupied by anxiety related to previous suicide \nattempt while on medical floor in the context of uncontrolled \npain. Patient had difficulty remembering details of this event. \nPatient's anxiety improved over course of hospitalization and \nendorsed safety while on floor. She was motivated to try \noutpatient management through a detox program at ___ and had \ndiscussed this plan with Dr. ___ pain management \nspecialist. After the team discussed case with Dr. ___ \ncontacted a Suboxone provider, Dr. ___ patient was given \nthe name and number, and patient agreed to contact.  At time of \ndischarge, patient had a scheduled appointment with Dr. ___, \nDr. ___ therapist, and Dr. ___. She also agreed to \ncall ___ regarding their detox program.\n \nAfter speaking with Dr. ___ was prescribed Methadone \n25mg total a day. She was receiving total of 30mg daily while in \nhospital.  She also told team that she was supposed to be taking \n50mg BID, as was reportedly recommended by Dr. ___ Dr. \n___ team that she is prescribed 50mg daily. ___ \ndid state, however, that she never actually started taking this \nmedication at home because she came to the hospital at the onset \nof her flare. \n\nAt time of discharge, patient reported that she needed a \nprescription for Methadone because Steph, her partner, had \nflushed all her Methadone in the toilet before coming to Deac 4, \nbelieving that she was going \"directly to a detox center.\" Dr. \n___ team that patient had used this same excuse \npreviously, asking for early refills of Methadone and Dilaudid. \nDr. ___ great concern for abuse of pain \nmedications and asked team not to prescribe any thing for \npatient, and that she be the only prescriber. Therefore, patient \nwas not discharged on any medicatons, and she was asked to stop \nby Dr. ___ for prescriptions if necessary. Upon \nspeaking with Steph at time of dicharge, Steph admits to \nflushing the Methadone down the toilet herself after discussing \nwhat to do with the medication with ___ at the onset of the \nflare. They believed this would be the best way to restrain \n___ access to the medication in the time of the flare and \non discharge from the hospital. An e-mail regarding this \ncommunication was sent to Dr. ___ at the time of discharge. \nAt time of discharge, patient contracted for safety, denied \nSI/HI, AVH and was goal directed regarding following up with her \noutpatient providers. No major medication changes were made \nduring this hospitalization and patient will be followed closely \nregarding her medication regimen by Dr. ___. \n\nDuring hospitalization, she was continued on:\n         Buspirone 10 mg PO TID\n         Amitriptyline 50 mg PO/NG HS \n         Mirtazapine 15 mg PO/NG HS  \n         Sertraline 50 mg PO/NG DAILY \n         Lorazepam 1 mg PO/NG Q4H:PRN anxiety \n         Zolpidem Tartrate 10 mg PO HS  \n\n#) Medical. Patient presented to ED at the onset of a \npancreatitis flare. No medication changes were made to her \nmedical/pain regimen and patient reported that pain was under \ncontrol. She was continued on: \n-Chronic Pancreatitis/Flare: \n         Clonidine 0.1mg PO BID\n         Methadone 10mg PO Q6H:PRN Pain (total of 30mg daily)\n         Acetaminophen-Caff-Butalbital ___ TAB PO Q6H:PRN pain \n         Phenergan 25 mg PO Q4H:PRN nausea\n         Ibuprofen 600mg prn \n         Pancrelipase 5000 1 cap PO QID\n         Tramadol 50mg PO BID \n         Tizanidine 8mg PO QHS prn pain\n         Tizanidine 2mg PO QAM prn pain\n         Gabapentin 400mg TID\n\n-GERD:\n         Pantoprazole 40mg PO Qdaily (home med)\n-HTN:\n         Lisinopril 10mg PO Qdaily (home med)\n         Metoprolol extended release 25mg PO Qdaily (home med)\n- Toothache:\n         Ibuprofen 600mg prn\n\n#)Safety: No acute safety concerns throughout hospitalization. \nShe was not a threat to herself or others. Patient was \nmaintained on Q15 minute checks.\n\n#) Legal status: Conditional Voluntary\n\n#) Psychosocial: She attended groups and received psychotherapy \nper unit routine.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nMood d/o NOS, hx of substance abuse",
